    "policy_organic_cotton_bottom": {
      "type": "policy",
      "blocks": {
        "item_what_is": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What organic cotton is",
            "text": "<p>Organic cotton is cotton grown without synthetic pesticides, synthetic fertilizers, or genetically modified seeds. Farmers use natural methods instead to protect the soil and the people working it. It's the same cotton, just grown differently — healthier soil, cleaner water runoff, and a farmer who didn't have to work with toxic chemicals.</p><p>Organic farming also protects soil health through crop rotation, rather than depleting it season after season.</p>",
            "heading_color": "secondary"
          }
        },
        "item_how_made": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How it's made",
            "text": "<p>After harvest, the raw cotton is ginned to remove seeds and debris, then spun into yarn. That yarn is woven or knitted into fabric, dyed, and cut and sewn into the finished garment.</p><p>Because no synthetic chemicals were used at the farming stage, organic cotton processing carries that principle forward — limiting harsh chlorine bleaches, toxic dyes, formaldehyde, and heavy metals at every later step, from spinning through finishing. The goal is a fabric that's clean end to end, not just at the field.</p>",
            "heading_color": "secondary"
          }
        },
        "item_verification": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How it's verified",
            "text": "<p>Organic cotton claims are checked through independent certification. Certifying bodies audit farms and factories every year, test soil samples, and trace the fiber from field to finished garment — confirming that no prohibited chemicals were used at any stage, from growing to dyeing to final stitching.</p>",
            "heading_color": "secondary"
          }
        },
        "item_why_we_sell": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why we sell it",
            "text": "<p>We sell clothing made predominantly from organic cotton, because it's better at every stage — for the soil it's grown in, for the people who grow and sew it, and for the body that wears it. Without residual pesticides or harsh processing chemicals, organic cotton also tends to be softer, more breathable, and gentler on sensitive skin.</p><p>But the main reason is this: behind the word \"organic\" is a specific, checkable promise — that this cotton was actually grown without synthetic pesticides. It's a smaller claim than most talk about \"sustainability\" and \"eco-friendliness,\" and we'd rather stick to it.</p>",
            "heading_color": "secondary"
          }
        }
      },
